# ~/.config/sway/config: Sway window manager configuration
# see https://swaywm.org/
#
# Install (canonical package set: setup/packages/desktop.list):
#   sudo apt install sway swaylock swaynag swayidle foot brightnessctl \
#     waybar rofi mako-notifier grim slurp grimshot flameshot playerctl \
#     network-manager-applet xdg-desktop-portal-wlr fonts-font-awesome \
#     jq wl-clipboard libnotify-bin pulseaudio-utils \
#     gnome-session-canberra sound-theme-freedesktop
# grimshot --notify needs a notification daemon (mako-notifier); the shutter
# sound needs canberra-gtk-play (gnome-session-canberra) + sound-theme-freedesktop.

# {{{ = Structure ============================================================
# This config is split into ordered fragments under config.d/, loaded in
# lexical order by the include below. Fragment order matters: variables
# (30-variables) must load before the key bindings and window rules that
# reference them ($mod, $ws*, $term, ...). To read the effective config as one
# stream: `cat ~/.config/sway/config.d/*.conf` (grep across them to connect
# variable definitions to their uses).
#
#   00-nvidia.conf         Nvidia driver notes (no live settings)
#   10-output-input.conf   Outputs (monitors), wallpaper, keyboard/pointer/touchpad
#   20-styles.conf         Font, borders, focus behavior, base16 colors, waybar
#   30-variables.conf      $mod/$hyper, workspaces, opacity, apps, window-state cmds
#   40-keybindings.conf    All bindsym + meta modes (window, system, pointer)
#   70-window-rules.conf   for_window/no_focus criteria, workspace assignment
#   90-launch-apps.conf    Startup exec + tray applets (after waybar)
#
# Sway resolves include paths relative to this file's directory and expands the
# glob in sorted (lexical) order, so the numeric prefixes fix the load order.
# Fragments are individual dotfiles symlinks (see AGENTS.md "Dotfiles
# Linking") -- run `dotfiles-link` after adding or renaming one.
# }}} = Structure ============================================================

include config.d/*.conf
